Package: yolo26-booth-demo
Version: __VERSION__
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: rickw00d <rickw00d@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: __SIZE__
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, fonts-noto-cjk, v4l-utils, curl, ca-certificates, xdg-utils
Homepage: https://github.com/rickw00d/Yolo26-booth-demo
Description: YOLO26 real-time AI vision booth demo
 Trade-show demo that runs real-time object detection, segmentation and
 pose estimation from a USB camera or a live stream, with a full-screen
 browser dashboard, face blur, an item challenge and on-device AI Q&A
 through Ollama. Built for NVIDIA GB10 (DGX Spark / MSI EdgeXpert).
 .
 Installation downloads PyTorch (CUDA 13), Python packages and the YOLO
 models, so it needs internet access and takes about 10-20 minutes.
